11. Database and performance engineering
Use Sequelize migrations as the source of truth for schema changes.
Do not rely on sequelize.sync({ force: true }) or destructive synchronization in production.
Requirements:
* Appropriate primary and foreign keys
* Tenant-aware composite indexes
* Unique constraints
* Query-efficient associations
* Transactions for multi-step business operations
* Safe pagination
* N+1 query prevention
* Select only required columns
* Explicit query limits
* Connection pooling
* Index design based on actual access patterns
* Efficient dashboard aggregates
* Background processing for expensive work
* Database query logging suitable for diagnostics
* Slow-query investigation guidance
* Backup and restore instructions
Avoid loading thousands of records into the frontend to implement search or pagination.
Use Redis caching only where it provides measured value. Tenant IDs and relevant permission context must be incorporated into cache keys and invalidation logic.
Document expected scalability limits and performance-test the important endpoints.
